# slugsmith

Small, dependency-free ESM library that turns titles into URL slugs. Published
to npm; `src/` is the whole public surface (`files` in `package.json`).

## Commands

- `npm test` runs the suite (`node --test`). Run one file with
  `npm test -- test/slug.test.js`.
- `npm run lint` checks tabs, trailing whitespace and stray `console.log`.
- Node 20+ is required.

A Stop hook runs `npm test` when you finish a turn and asks you to keep going
if it fails. Fix the failure; don't disable the hook.

## Conventions

@docs/conventions.md

## Gotchas

- Explicit rules in `src/rules.js` run before accent stripping, so `ö` becomes
  `oe`, not `o`. Changing that order changes existing slugs.
- Slugs are part of users' URLs. Any change to existing output is a breaking
  change and needs a major version bump.
- Never read or edit `.env`; it holds the npm publish token. Use
  `.env.example` for the variable names.

## Personal settings

Put machine-specific notes in `CLAUDE.local.md`, which is gitignored.
